## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Spoken Books
## Notes: Books, letters and notes read aloud through the Spoken player.
## Version: 2.0.0
## Author: rusty
## SavedVariables: SpokenBooksDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: SpokenBooksCharDB
# Two tables, because they answer different questions. SpokenBooksDB is how you like the
# addon to behave and is yours; SpokenBooksCharDB is what a particular character has heard,
# so an alt walking into the same library is read to rather than met with silence.
## OptionalDeps: SpokenPlayer, SpokenBooksAudio
# SpokenPlayer is the player this addon speaks through. Optional here so a hand-installed
# copy without it loads and says what is missing rather than failing to load at all; addon
# managers install it from the CurseForge dependency. The pack is not a registration
# mechanism either -- it registers itself into SpokenBooksAudioPacks and Audio.lua walks
# that on demand -- so this list is load order only.
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\SpokenBooks\Textures\AddonIcon.tga
## X-License: Addon code MIT. Book text is Blizzard's, extracted from the game.

Checksum.lua
Data/Books.lua
Core.lua
Reader.lua
Contribute.lua
Audio.lua
Playlist.lua
UI/Layout.lua
UI/Options.lua
UI/PlayButton.lua
UI/CopyLink.lua
Events.lua
Commands.lua

# UI/Layout.lua is byte-identical in every Spoken addon and must stay that way -- the file
# says why, and pipelines/quests/tests/test_package.py is what enforces it. It loads before
# UI/Options.lua, which builds its panel with it, and both load before Events.lua, which is
# what calls SetupOptions once the world is up.
